<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Defenders of the Homeland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1943–1945</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Pembela Tanah Air</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Defenders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">Homeland</a>, known as PETA, was a volunteer army of Indonesians raised by the Japanese occupiers in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> in October 1943 to help resist an Allied invasion. Its units revolted at Blitar in February 1945. Disbanded after the Japanese surrender, it provided many officers of the new Indonesian army, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudirman">Sudirman</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suharto">Suharto</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/defenders-of-the-homeland.jpg" alt="Defenders of the Homeland" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pembela Tanah Air, Vectorization: Jeromi Mikhael · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_PETA_(Pembela_Tanah_Air).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
